{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that each parameter (`alpha`, `beta`, and `sigma`) receives its built-in prior sampling statement before being used in the likelihood for the protected observation `y`. The posterior/log density is otherwise unchanged. No data fields were added or changed; `x` remains an unprotected context predictor and `N` remains a size input.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real alpha;
  real beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 10);
  y ~ normal(alpha + beta * x, sigma);
}
generated quantities {
  array[N] real y_rep = normal_rng(alpha + beta * x, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"x":[4.653280430879779,2.9948658049511248,2.1392647478059974],"y":[3.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
